   $q$In paragraph 1, Lena's legs felt "as wobbly as cooked noodles." What does this simile tell you?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Her legs felt weak and shaky on the ice.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Her legs felt warm after eating lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Her legs felt strong and ready to race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Her legs felt long and thin like pasta.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her legs felt weak and shaky on the ice.$q$, $q$Cooked noodles are soft and floppy, so the simile shows Lena's legs were shaky and unsteady. It compares how her legs felt, not how they looked or anything she ate.$q$, 'draft', '471a7fff-920b-5db7-a545-36572ab784df')
