   $q$In paragraph 6, Grandpa Teo says, "You have a knack for this." What does "have a knack for" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to have a natural skill at doing something","is_correct":true},{"text":"to have trouble learning something new","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"to have a small tool for shaping the clay","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"to have a habit of making a lot of mess","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to have a natural skill at doing something$q$, $q$He says this after Mia makes her first bowl, so he is praising her skill. A knack is not a tool, and he is not saying she struggles.$q$, 'draft', 'dd336eed-36a2-5926-b347-1e1ed06c54c6')
