   $q$In paragraph 5, the author uses the saying "you have to spend money to make money." What does it mean about solar panels?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Families should never buy anything that costs a lot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Paying a lot at first can help families save money later.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Solar panels are cheap, so families never spend much.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Families get paid by the Sun for using solar panels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Paying a lot at first can help families save money later.$q$, $q$The paragraph says panels "cost a lot of money" but "can save families money" on bills over time. The saying explains that spending first leads to a gain later; it does not say the panels are cheap.$q$, 'draft', '51875581-56e4-51ee-b6f8-322c64214379')
