   $q$In the last paragraph, Diego "felt as proud as a peacock." What does this simile mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He felt very pleased with what he did.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He wanted to visit birds at the zoo.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He felt sad that he lost one game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"He wore a shirt covered in feathers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He felt very pleased with what he did.$q$, $q$A peacock shows off its feathers proudly, and Diego is holding the ribbon he earned. The simile is about his feeling, not about real feathers.$q$, 'draft', '1f73fa7e-1c17-520a-bdd3-2901fea54021')
